rld/collab/exception-track/1794241000000-engineer-donor-link-absent.gemini-3.8-flash-high.findings.md) and [`collab/yang-clojure/1794217000000-codex-cc1-regate2.findings.md`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/yang-clojure/1794217000000-codex-cc1-regate2.findings.md).\nI will now read [`collab/dao-stream/1794955000000-orchestrator-to-daostream-batch-cljs-failures.md`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/dao-stream/1794955000000-orchestrator-to-daostream-batch-cljs-failures.md) and the rest of the grep results to see the full context of the C1 design and the `dao.stream` cljs failure.\nI will now locate and read the Addendum A / attribution-as-query ruling documents in `collab/yang-clojure/`.\nI will now read [`1794600000000-architect-attribution-as-query-ruling-of-record.md`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/yang-clojure/1794600000000-architect-attribution-as-query-ruling-of-record.md), [`1794630000000-architect-attribution-addendum-a-RECORD.md`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/yang-clojure/1794630000000-architect-attribution-addendum-a-RECORD.md), and [`1794670000000-architect-callsite-generalization-design.gpt-6-astra.findings.md`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/yang-clojure/1794670000000-architect-callsite-generalization-design.gpt-6-astra.findings.md).\nCompleted-GMT: 2026-11-09 19:39:00 UTC\nCompleted-Local: 2026-11-10 02:39:00 +0700\n\n# Architect Ruling: `cc1` Cross-Host Publication Regression (`b1b9abae`)\n\n---\n\n## 1. Host-Independence Audit \u0026 True Cause of the Regression\n\n### 1.1 Audit of the Inspected Pipeline (`macro.cljc`, `publish.cljc`, `linker.cljc`, `closure.cljc`, `jing.cljc`, `cbor.cljc`)\n\n1. **CBOR canonical encoder ([`dao.jing`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/dao/jing.cljc#L1-L120), [`dao.jing.cbor`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/dao/jing/cbor.cljc#L1-L58)):**\n   - [`dao.jing/materialize!`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/dao/jing.cljc#L1-L35) encodes maps and sets into canonical RFC 8949 byte-sorted order via [`dao.jing.cbor/encode`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/dao/jing/cbor.cljc#L11-L26) and hashes the canonical byte array with BLAKE3. Map/set iteration order on the host cannot cause hash drift once a map or set reaches `dao.jing.cbor`.\n   - **Vectors, however, are positional in CBOR** (`dao.jing.cbor` encodes vectors as plain CBOR arrays in their existing element order). Any vector materialized as a blob (such as the C1 call-site side table) must therefore be deterministically ordered *before* reaching `jing/materialize!`.\n\n2. **Call-site table \u0026 record construction ([`yin.vm.linker.publish`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/linker/publish.cljc#L129-L263), [`yang.clojure`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc#L105-L115), [`yin.vm.macro`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/macro.cljc#L670-L715)):**\n   - **Default admission token ([`default-admission-token`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/linker/publish.cljc#L140-L157)):** When neither `:yin.link.publish/admission` nor `:yin.link.publish/scope` is supplied in `composition`, the token is `[:yin.link.publish/default-admission (jing/segment-key {:yin.link.publish/name ... :yin.link.publish/root ... :yin.link.publish/exports ... :yin.link.publish/requires ... :yin.link.publish/primitives ...})]`. Because `jing/segment-key` hashes canonical CBOR bytes, the default admission origin `[:source :yin.vm.linker.publish/publish token 0]` is **identical across JVM, Node, and Dart** for identical inputs. (Mutable counter state only enters when a caller explicitly supplies [`admission-scope`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/linker/publish.cljc#L160-L176).)\n   - **Expander lineage tracking ([`yin.vm.macro/register-lineage!`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/macro.cljc#L670-L715), [`final-call-site-metadata`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/macro.cljc#L1598-L1626)):** `lineage-origin-for` uses `identical?` on `(:rows entry)` only to distinguish an in-memory retained packet from a content-twin packet within a single macro step, and falls back to unique `[root rows]` matching when unambiguous. None of `::origin-of` or `:packet-lineage` escapes into serialized rows ([`strip-packet-tracking`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/macro.cljc#L718-L735)).\n   - **Row sorting ([`call-site-claim`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/linker/publish.cljc#L213), [`yang.clojure/call-site-metadata`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc#L112), [`yin.vm.macro/dedupe-call-site-rows`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/macro.cljc#L1387)):** All three places deduplicate with `(distinct)` and sort the call-site rows `[origin root-address path :yang/call-site 1]` using `(vec (sort-by pr-str ...))`. For the current origin/root/path vocabulary (keywords, strings, non-negative integers), `pr-str` happens to produce identical strings on JVM and Node, though using `pr-str` as a canonical comparator is a latent cross-host defect (see §2 below).\n\n3. **Why [`yang.python.antlr.dht-import-test`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/test/yang/python/antlr/dht_import_test.cljc#L1-L265) actually failed on `b1b9abae`:**\n   - The failure is **not** JVM-vs-Node hash divergence at runtime; it is **manifest content-hash contamination between live `(fixture/generate)` after `cc1` and the checked-in pre-`cc1` golden corpus [`test/resources/yang/python/dht-import-v1.edn`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/test/resources/yang/python/dht-import-v1.edn)**:\n     1. In [`yang.core.call/module-uast`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yang/core/call.cljc#L168-L175), `cc1` (`fa70516f`) annotated the shared `yang.call` module AST with `(u/annotate-call-sites ...)`.\n     2. In [`yin.vm.linker.publish/publish-closure!`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/linker/publish.cljc#L351-L363), `cc1` (`f440a2fb` / `ba2deb73`) injected `:yin.module/call-sites {:table (:table call-sites) :record (:record call-sites)}` **directly into the hashed module manifest**.\n     3. When [`yang.python.antlr.linked-harness/published`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/test/yang/python/antlr/linked_harness.cljc#L55-L64) publishes `yang.call`, its manifest now contains `:yin.module/call-sites`, changing `(:call-address @h/published)` away from the pre-`cc1` address `:segment/blake3-ef21320944b651140c11dedebd8b443fb91d32f99678f9c274568fbe4d07eea4`.\n     4. Because the Python prelude `py` pins `:yin.module/requires {'yang.call call-address}`, `py`'s manifest address (`(:address @h/published)`) also changed (breaking [`manifest-golden`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/test/yang/python/antlr/linked_prelude_test.cljc#L229-L249) `:segment/blake3-d9aead51dc2da70f8dcd8935f2a8c3bc052037967064b45d1914897ad03a6a9c`).\n     5. Because every guest Python module (`pym.m`, `pym.k`, `pym.t`, `pym.e`, and `k2`) in [`yang.python.antlr.dht-import-fixture/generate`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/test/yang/python/antlr/dht_import_fixture.cljc#L120-L162) pins `:requires {'py py-address, 'yang.call call-address}`, every guest module's manifest address, site-set record (`:yang.site/manifest`), and signed publication envelope changed at runtime.\n     6. Both [`dht-import-test-test`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/test/yang/python/antlr/dht_import_test.cljc#L254-L265) and [`manifest-address-test`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/test/yang/python/antlr/linked_prelude_test.cljc#L240-L249) are marked `^:slow`. `cc1` only ran the JVM quick lane (`-e :slow`), skipping both tests and leaving `test/resources/yang/python/dht-import-v1.edn` untouched.\n     7. When the Node slow lane ran `dht-import-test`:\n        - [`this-host-publishes-the-artifact`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/test/yang/python/antlr/dht_import_test.cljc#L61-L82) compared `(fixture/parse artifact-lines)` (read from the committed pre-`cc1` `dht-import-v1.edn`) against live `(fixture/generate)`. The reported `:blobs-differ [\":segment/blake3-00f50692...\" \":segment/blake3-13ba...\"]` are line 10 (`pym.t`'s pre-`cc1` manifest) and line 19 (`k2`'s pre-`cc1` site-set record) from `dht-import-v1.edn`.\n        - Then [`publish-world`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/test/yang/python/antlr/dht_import_test.cljc#L36-L58) seeded the mesh nodes with `(fixture/installed-py)` (the **post-`cc1`** `py` and `yang.call` closures) while loading the **pre-`cc1`** guest blobs from `dht-import-v1.edn` (which require the old `py` and `yang.call` addresses that no node in the mesh holds). Every subsequent DHT link step failed to resolve `py` / `yang.call`, producing the 84 assertion failures and 3 unreached assertions (`158 → 155`, inside [`a-hook-import-chain`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/test/yang/python/antlr/dht_import_test.cljc#L168-L194) when `rebound` is nil).\n\n---\n\n## 2. Ruling: **(c) Both, for Different Parts** — Primary **(b) Exclude** `:yin.module/call-sites` from the Hashed Module Manifest, Plus **(a) Canonicalize** the Side-Table Row Comparator\n\n### Part B (Primary): **Exclude** `:yin.module/call-sites` from the Schema-1 Hashed Module Manifest\n\n1. **Where to exclude:**\n   - **[`src/cljc/yin/vm/linker/publish.cljc`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/linker/publish.cljc#L327-L370) (`publish-closure!`):** Remove `:yin.module/call-sites` from `manifest`. Do **not** `assoc` `{:table (:table call-sites) :record (:record call-sites)}` into the manifest map that is passed to `jing/materialize!`.\n   - **[`src/cljc/yin/vm/linker.cljc`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/linker.cljc#L739-L845) (`manifest-keys`, `manifest-defect`):** Revert `:yin.module/call-sites` from `manifest-keys` and `manifest-defect`. Schema-1 `manifest-keys` remains the closed 10-key set (`#{:yin.module/name :yin.module/schema :yin.module/contracts :yin.module/tree :yin.module/derivations :yin.module/index :yin.module/exports :yin.module/requires :yin.module/primitives :yin.module/footprint}`).\n   - **[`src/cljc/yin/vm/linker/closure.cljc`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/linker/closure.cljc#L130-L157) (`walk-call-sites`, `walk-manifest`):** Revert `walk-call-sites` from `walk-manifest`. Code-execution closure walks only the manifest, its canonical tree, its derivations, its optional `:yin.module/index`, and its `:yin.module/requires` manifests.\n   - **[`src/cljc/yin/vm/linker/publish.cljc`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/linker/publish.cljc#L218-L263) (`call-site-record`, `publish-call-sites!`, `published-call-site-table`):** Invert the pointer direction to match [`yang.python.antlr.siteset/record`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yang/python/antlr/siteset.cljc#L79-L101):\n     - Materialize the module manifest **first** to obtain `manifest-address`.\n     - When `(claims-call-sites? ast)` is true, construct the call-site publication record so that **the record names the manifest**:\n       ```clojure\n       {:yang.call-site/schema   1\n        :yang.call-site/manifest manifest-address\n        :yang.call-site/root     (:root tree)\n        :yang.call-site/origin   origin\n        :yang.call-site/table    table-address}\n       ```\n     - Materialize `table` and `record` into `handle` and return `:call-sites {:record record-address :table table-address :origin origin :root (:root tree) :manifest manifest-address}` in the result map of `publish-module!`.\n     - For `published-call-site-table`, accept either the `:record` address directly (or the `publish-module!` result map / a caller-supplied record address) or resolve a side association, validating that `(:yang.call-site/manifest record) = manifest-address` and `(:yang.call-site/root record) = (:yin.module/tree manifest)`.\n\n2. **What the design loses by excluding `:yin.module/call-sites` from the hashed manifest (and why that is intentional):**\n   - A bare `manifest-address` alone no longer suffices for `yin.vm.linker.closure/walk` to pull the call-site side table during an execution-only module load, nor can `published-call-site-table` discover the side-table address solely by reading `(jing/get handle manifest-address)` without the call-site record address (or an index entry `[e :yang.call-site/manifest manifest-address]` / `[e :yang.call-site/record record-address]`, exactly as `yang.python.antlr.siteset` does for `:yang.site/manifest`).\n   - **Nothing in execution semantics is lost** because evaluators and linkers never consult C1 call-site tables to execute code; C1 is strictly query/attribution provenance metadata.\n\n### Part A (Secondary): **Canonicalize** the Call-Site Side-Table Row Ordering\n\n- **Where to canonicalize:**\n  - [`src/cljc/yin/vm/linker/publish.cljc`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/linker/publish.cljc#L213) (`call-site-claim`)\n  - [`src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc#L112) (`call-site-metadata`)\n  - [`src/cljc/yin/vm/macro.cljc`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/macro.cljc#L1387) (`dedupe-call-site-rows` at line 1387 and `final-call-site-metadata` at line 1622)\n- **How:** Replace `(sort-by pr-str ...)` with a deterministic structural tuple comparator over `[origin root-address path :yang/call-site version]` (or `sort-by jing/canonical-bytes` with byte-wise comparison), so the materialized `:table` vector never depends on host `pr-str` formatting or string-lexicographic integer ordering (`\"[10]\"` \u003c `\"[2]\"`).\n\n---\n\n## 3. Architectural Reasons from the Design\n\n1. **Occurrence Identity vs. Content Identity \u0026 Unitarity ([`1795310000000-owner-ruling-occurrence-identity-unitarity.md`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/yang-clojure/1795310000000-owner-ruling-occurrence-identity-unitarity.md) U1–U3; [`1794630000000-architect-attribution-addendum-a-RECORD.md`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/yang-clojure/1794630000000-architect-attribution-addendum-a-RECORD.md) §A1; `docs/design/yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md ~:659`):**\n   - Addendum A §A1 explicitly states: *\"The existing architecture defines a call site as `[origin root-address path]` and **excludes provenance from hashed code content** (`docs/design/yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md ~:659`).\"*\n   - Under Owner Ruling U1–U2, `:yang.call-site/origin` (`[:source :yin.vm.linker.publish/publish token 0]`) is the identity of the **admission event**, not of the compiled code. When two admissions publish the exact same module specification under distinct scopes (`:yin.link.publish/scope`), their `:origin`, `:table`, and `:record` addresses are intentionally distinct (`1794670000000` §5.2: *\"admits identical text twice with distinct supplied admission tokens and demands different origins. Cross-host equality is replay equality; it must not turn occurrences into content identities\"*).\n   - By embedding `:yin.module/call-sites {:table ... :record ...}` inside the hashed manifest, `cc1` caused **identical module specifications admitted under two scopes to produce different module manifest addresses**, and caused any change in call-site annotation on a base module (`yang.call`) to cascade through `:yin.module/requires` into the content addresses of every downstream prelude (`py`, `clj`) and guest module (`pym.*`).\n\n2. **Closed Schema-1 Module Manifest Contract ([`1794600000000-architect-attribution-as-query-ruling-of-record.md`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/yang-clojure/1794600000000-architect-attribution-as-query-ruling-of-record.md) line 62; [`1794630000000-architect-attribution-addendum-a-RECORD.md`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/yang-clojure/1794630000000-architect-attribution-addendum-a-RECORD.md) §A2; [`1794670000000-architect-callsite-generalization-design.gpt-6-astra.findings.md`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/yang-clojure/1794670000000-architect-callsite-generalization-design.gpt-6-astra.findings.md) §3.1 \u0026 §4.2):**\n   - Ruling of Record Scoping Inventory (line 62):\n     `| Manifest schema | schema-1, CLOSED key set | nothing (linkage evidence is out-of-band; schema-2 only if R1's durable record later lands) |`\n   - Approved C1/D1 Design (`1794670000000` §3.1 line 117):\n     `| Linker manifest | Keep schema 1 by publishing correspondence beside it. | Adding a manifest field requires a separately versioned manifest contract and validator; current closed keys reject it. No automatic schema-2 just because R1 is now active. |`\n   - Approved C1/D1 Design (`1794670000000` §4.2 line 223):\n     *\"The Python site-set record is a concrete precedent for 'record names manifest, manifest keeps schema' (`siteset.cljc:5-22,79-101`).\"*\n\n3. **Precedent in [`yang.python.antlr.siteset`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yang/python/antlr/siteset.cljc#L5-L14) (`docs/design/yin.repl.dao.space-index.md`, `docs/design/yin.vm.linker.dht.md`):**\n   - `siteset.cljc` states the invariant verbatim: *\"Site marks never enter canonical rows, so a published module tree carries none; they live in the frontend-metadata side table... A separate publication record, keyed by the module's manifest address, pins the association... **The module manifest keeps its schema: a manifest address names code, and a record names a manifest.**\"*\n\n---\n\n## 4. Acceptance Test \u0026 Non-Regression Gates\n\n1. **Tests that must go green without regenerating golden fixtures:**\n   - **[`yang.python.antlr.dht-import-test`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/test/yang/python/antlr/dht_import_test.cljc):** All 5 `deftest`s (`dht-import-test-test`), **158 assertions, 0 failures, 0 errors** on both JVM and Node (and Dart), against the existing committed [`test/resources/yang/python/dht-import-v1.edn`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/test/resources/yang/python/dht-import-v1.edn) **without regenerating `dht-import-v1.edn`**.\n   - **[`yang.python.antlr.linked-prelude-test`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/test/yang/python/antlr/linked_prelude_test.cljc):** `manifest-address-test` (`^:slow`) must pass with the existing golden manifest address `:segment/blake3-d9aead51dc2da70f8dcd8935f2a8c3bc052037967064b45d1914897ad03a6a9c` and `yang.call` address `:segment/blake3-ef21320944b651140c11dedebd8b443fb91d32f99678f9c274568fbe4d07eea4`.\n   - **[`yang.clojure-callsite-test`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/test/yang/clojure_callsite_test.cljc):** All C1 coverage, macro packet provenance (`p1-packet-provenance-test`, `twin-identical-content-distinct-origin-test`), and publication tests (`published-module-test`, `publisher-scope-admission-identity-test`, `publisher-scope-id-identity-test`) must pass, updated only where `published-module-test` previously asserted `(:yin.module/call-sites manifest)` inside the manifest so that it instead asserts:\n     - `(= (:address via-a) (:address via-b))` (identical module specifications under different admission scopes produce the **same** module manifest address), while\n     - `(not= (get-in via-a [:call-sites :origin]) (get-in via-b [:call-sites :origin]))` and `(not= (get-in via-a [:call-sites :record]) (get-in via-b [:call-sites :record]))` (their call-site records and tables remain distinct per admission and each record's `:yang.call-site/manifest` pins that manifest address).\n\n2. **What must NOT change:**\n   - [`test/resources/yang/python/dht-import-v1.edn`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/test/resources/yang/python/dht-import-v1.edn) and [`manifest-golden`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/test/yang/python/antlr/linked_prelude_test.cljc#L229-L238) must **not** be rewritten to paper over manifest hash drift.\n   - Schema-1 [`yin.vm.linker/manifest-keys`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/linker.cljc#L739-L745) must remain the closed 10-key set without `:yin.module/call-sites`.\n   - [`yang.core.call/module-uast`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yang/core/call.cljc#L168-L175) **keeps** `(u/annotate-call-sites ...)` — because canonical UAST rows strip `:yang/call-site` and the schema-1 manifest excludes `:yin.module/call-sites`, keeping `yang.call` annotated no longer alters its manifest address.\n\n3. **Status of sibling failure `dao.stream.ws-project-cross-node-test/corpus-jvm-serves-node-decodes-over-cbor`:**\n   - **Unrelated to `cc1`.** Inspection of [`test/dao/stream/ws_project_cross_node_test.cljs`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/test/dao/stream/ws_project_cross_node_test.cljs) and [`test/dao/stream/ws_project_corpus.cljc`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/test/dao/stream/ws_project_corpus.cljc) confirms it touches zero `yin.vm`, `yang.*`, or linker symbols (`jing-payload` is the static map `{:jing/probe [1 \"two\" :three]}`). It belongs to the `dao.stream` seat (`120ff322`), as already tracked in [`collab/dao-stream/1794955000000-orchestrator-to-daostream-batch-cljs-failures.md`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/dao-stream/1794955000000-orchestrator-to-daostream-batch-cljs-failures.md).\n","duration_seconds":848.050071,"num_turns":1,"usage":{"input_tokens":329934,"output_tokens":36598,"thinking_tokens":15955,"cache_read_tokens":5140658,"total_tokens":366532}}
